<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaoyou</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gaoyou is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiangsu">Jiangsu</a> province, eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-canal">Grand Canal</a> beside Gaoyou Lake. In 1354 the rebel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhang-shicheng">Zhang Shicheng</a> proclaimed his kingdom of Great Zhou there, and a large Yuan army under the chancellor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toghto">Toghto</a> besieged it until Toghto's sudden dismissal broke up the army, a turning point in the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan dynasty</a>. The city was the home of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> Guan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gaoyou.jpg" alt="Gaoyou" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Huangchenhai · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Haichao_Bridge_north.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
